{"parentUuid":"1eb3a341-7cbf-4d7b-a7eb-e0cafb635bc7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Ng4Trz4WCNCBoxstqm8jac","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — significant news. Codex got real `PostToolUse` for file edits in the last few months, and `entire`'s Codex integration hasn't picked it up yet.\n\n## What Codex now exposes\n\n`HookEventName` in latest `main` (`codex-rs/protocol/src/protocol.rs:1456`):\n\n```rust\nPreToolUse, PermissionRequest, PostToolUse,\nPreCompact, PostCompact,\nSessionStart, UserPromptSubmit, Stop,\n```\n\nCompare to what `entire/cli/agent/codex/lifecycle.go` currently registers: `session-start`, `user-prompt-submit`, `stop`, and a no-op `pre-tool-use`. **Half the lifecycle is unobserved.**\n\n## The fix that closes our gap\n\n`#18391 — fix(core): emit hooks for apply_patch edits` (commit `09ebc34f17`, 2026-04-21):\n\n> apply_patch is Codex's primary file edit path, but it was not emitting PreToolUse or PostToolUse hook events. … Added PreToolUse and PostToolUse payload support to ApplyPatchHandler. Exposed the raw patch body as `tool_input.command` for both JSON/function and freeform apply_patch calls.\n\nBefore this, even if you wired PostToolUse, you'd only see `Bash` shell calls — file mutations went silent. Now `apply_patch` emits a payload with the full patch envelope.\n\n## Payload shape\n\nWhen PostToolUse fires for a patch, the hook command receives this on stdin (`PostToolUseCommandInput` in `codex-rs/hooks/src/schema.rs:279`):\n\n```json\n{\n  \"session_id\": \"...\",\n  \"turn_id\": \"...\",\n  \"transcript_path\": \"/path/to/rollout.jsonl\",\n  \"cwd\": \"...\",\n  \"hook_event_name\": \"PostToolUse\",\n  \"tool_name\": \"apply_patch\",\n  \"tool_use_id\": \"call-...\",\n  \"tool_input\": {\n    \"command\": \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: foo.txt\\n@@\\n-bar\\n+baz\\n*** End Patch\\n\"\n  },\n  \"tool_response\": \"Success. Updated files.\"\n}\n```\n\nConfirmed by `apply_patch_tests.rs:82-99`. Matcher aliases `Write` and `Edit` also select apply_patch handlers (`hook_names.rs:34-39`), so Claude-style configs work too.\n\n## What this gives us\n\nWe can stop relying on `extractModifiedFilesFromLiveTranscript` (parses the whole rollout JSONL post-hoc) and populate `state.FilesTouched` incrementally during the turn, the same way Claude Code's PostToolUse path does. **That kills the carry-forward bug at its root**: with `state.FilesTouched` accurate, `resolveFilesTouched` returns the actual list, `filesWithRemainingAgentChanges` doesn't pick up scratch files, and `carryForwardToNewShadowBranch` doesn't fire spuriously.\n\n## Implementation sketch\n\nIt's small. Three changes inside `cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex/`:\n\n1. **`lifecycle.go`** — add `HookNamePostToolUse = \"post-tool-use\"` and a `parsePostToolUse(stdin)` returning a new `agent.Event` type (e.g. `agent.ToolUse` with `FilesTouched` field — Claude Code already has this shape; check how it merges).\n2. **`hooks.go`** — install a fourth hook command (`entire hooks codex post-tool-use`) under the `PostToolUse` event in `.codex/hooks.json`. No matcher (or matcher = `apply_patch`) — Bash payloads are useless for file tracking.\n3. **`transcript.go`** — already has `extractFilesFromApplyPatch(string) []string` parsing `*** {Add,Update,Delete} File:`. Reuse it on the hook stdin's `tool_input.command`.\n\nThe merge-into-`state.FilesTouched` plumbing already exists strategy-side — Claude Code's PostToolUse uses it, so it's just dispatching the new event type through `lifecycle.go`'s normalized event handling.\n\nOne caveat: requires `features.codex_hooks = true` in `.codex/config.toml` (which `ensureProjectFeatureEnabled` already writes), and a Codex build from after Apr 21, 2026. Older Codex versions silently won't fire the event — same fail-mode as today, so safe.\n\nWant me to write the patch?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":