{"parentUuid":"c1fea439-6318-4cb5-95a6-597a4ddb0e4f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_017pNHvwfPsM5gm5WPjdwe5N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Track Codex `apply_patch` mid-turn + serialize all session-state writes\n\nWhen Codex commits mid-turn (which it routinely does), the previous strategy had no per-tool file accounting — `state.FilesTouched` stayed empty until the Stop hook, so PostCommit's carry-forward decision fell back to whole-transcript extraction, over-reported \"remaining\" files, and reset `CheckpointTranscriptStart` to 0 on the next checkpoint. Two same-session checkpoints both showed `start=0` even though the transcript was cumulative.\n\n### What this PR does\n\n**Wires Codex's PostToolUse hook through to `state.FilesTouched`.** Codex (post-#18391) emits PostToolUse for every `apply_patch` with the patch envelope in `tool_input.command`. We now install a fourth hook command, parse the envelope (Add/Update/Delete plus `*** Move to:` renames), and merge paths via a new `agent.ToolUse` lifecycle event — so PostCommit sees an accurate file list and the carry-forward logic stops firing spuriously.\n\n**Funnels every session-state mutation through `MutateSessionState`.** PostToolUse fires at high frequency and Codex parallelizes tool calls. To eliminate lost-update races against TurnEnd / PostCommit / condense / model update / review-env / SessionEnd / etc., every load-modify-save in the lifecycle dispatcher and strategy package now goes through one helper that takes an OS flock against `.git/entire-session-locks/<id>.lock` for the load+fn+save. A per-process gate keyed by goroutine ID layers on top so nested calls in the same goroutine share the outer's state pointer rather than deadlocking on a second flock or losing inner updates to the outer save.\n\n### Notable bits\n- Lock files live in a sibling dir (`entire-session-locks/`) so session listings don't see them, and `ClearSessionState` deliberately doesn't unlink them (flock + unlink + recreate would lose mutual exclusion).\n- `initializeSession` re-checks under the lock to avoid a TOCTOU that would overwrite a richer concurrent state with blanks.\n- `SessionMetadata.CheckpointTranscriptStart` exposed in e2e testutil for future agent-validation tests.\n\n### Tests\n- Codex parser: apply_patch + Write/Edit aliases, non-mutating tools, empty patch, missing tool_input, Move-to renames, mixed siblings.\n- Strategy: parallel `RecordFilesTouched` merges across 20 goroutines; nested `MutateSessionState` calls reentrant in the same goroutine; `ClearSessionState` preserves the lock file; `MutateSessionState` doesn't clobber a richer state under a TOCTOU race.\n- Integration: `entire hooks codex post-tool-use` populates `state.FilesTouched` end-to-end; non-mutating tools are no-ops.\n\n`mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` all green."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":390,"cache_read_input_tokens":795868,"output_tokens":1024,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":390,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":1024,"cache_read_input_tokens":795868,"cache_creation_input_tokens":390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":390},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CapzXKHWTp1KZnikPknmp","type":"assistant","uuid":"1db33b7b-e8c3-4ea2-9353-c61d147c0b81","timestamp":"2026-05-08T11:05:46.503Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"b1ed7d58-eb6b-498c-931f-1f6f207e13c3","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"soph/add-codex-post-tool"}
