{"parentUuid":"5b256d5d-1fb4-46d3-beea-a422d718504b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Jyt3Z6oS8dQGGvya86oDvx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You've spotted a real chicken-and-egg. Trace:\n\n1. User runs `entire enable --agent codex` → sees the hint we added\n2. User starts codex → codex blocks the SessionStart hook (untrusted)\n3. `entire hooks codex session-start` never runs → `WriteHookResponse(\"Entire CLI will link this conversation to your next commit.\")` never fires\n4. User sees codex's own warning but **not** our welcome banner\n5. User runs `/hooks`, trusts, restarts codex → from this session forward, the welcome banner fires normally\n\nSo the welcome banner is **silent for the entire pre-trust window**. There's no path to deliver it that doesn't go through a hook.\n\nThe mitigation we have is just the install-time hint, which has a coverage gap: it fires only when `installedHooks > 0`. So:\n- **First `entire enable` on a machine** → hint shows ✓\n- **Cloning a repo where someone else already committed `.codex/hooks.json`** → `entire enable` is a no-op (count=0), hint doesn't fire, user has no idea entire is integrated until codex warns them about untrusted hooks\n- **Same user, same repo, second machine** → same as the clone case (trust is per-user, hooks are per-repo)\n\nCodex's own warning fills the gap (`⚠ N hooks need review. Open /hooks`), but it's generic — it doesn't tell the user *what* `entire hooks codex session-start` is or why they should trust it. They have to take it on faith from the command name.\n\nOptions if you want to close this gap:\n\n**A) Always print the hint when codex hooks are present**, not only when `installedHooks > 0`. Drops the no-op-quiet behavior on re-runs but covers the clone case.\n\n**B) Detect untrusted hooks** at `entire enable` time by parsing `~/.codex/config.toml` for `trusted_hash` entries matching our keys. Print the hint only when actually untrusted. Brittle (replicates Codex's hashing, same fragility we already discussed).\n\n**C) Print a one-line \"what entire does\" line in the post-install hint**, so even users who never see the SessionStart welcome know what they're trusting:\n```\nCodex 0.129+ requires you to approve new hooks once. Run /hooks inside\nCodex to trust them — until you do, Entire CLI's commit checkpointing\nstays inactive.\n```\n\n**D) Add a `entire status` (or similar entry-point) check** that warns when codex hooks exist locally but the user's `~/.codex/config.toml` lacks trust entries. Surfaces on any `entire` invocation in a Codex repo.\n\nMy read: **A + C** is the smallest correct fix. It guarantees every Codex-using machine sees the hint at least once on `entire enable`, and the wording is honest about the consequence. Want me to do that?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1358,"cache_read_input_tokens":888841,"output_tokens":3644,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1358,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3644,"cache_read_input_tokens":888841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1358},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caq94KQkUYzeomp53vaci","type":"assistant","uuid":"08b9a558-e764-4ced-b34f-5ec8ebc96edb","timestamp":"2026-05-08T12:58:14.620Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"b1ed7d58-eb6b-498c-931f-1f6f207e13c3","version":"2.1.129","gitBranch":"soph/add-codex-post-tool"}
